{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/271310-looking-for-st-for-vtm-requiem-or-forsaken-game","id":271310,"title":"Looking for ST for VtM, Requiem, or Forsaken game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-02T19:36:18-07:00","id":271310,"title":"Looking for ST for VtM, Requiem, or Forsaken game.","content":"So there are a few threads that are close but getting mixed groups, or are pretty old/defunct. Therefore to put the official feeler out.<br /> <br /> I have a group of players (about 4 depending on the game.) Who are interested in a regular game. We would need an ST who can run this online, preferably skype as everyone is currently on skype, but if that doesn't work, then we can certainly look at switching playing venue. Interest would be in either Vampire as a Masquerade game that allows Cam vampires (preferably Revised Masq since lets face it V20 still has a lot of stuff left to publish before it comes close to OWoD.) or a Requiem game. Another option would be Werewolf the Forsaken as a venue of interest as the players were part of a pack on a chat who's Forsaken venue fell apart.<br /> <br /> The players are fairly easy going and are good gamers of various stripes/genres and one thing we need is an ST who is stable and can actually run a regular game over a long term. There are of course no shortage of folks wanting to ST, just a shortage of folks who can put rubber to road. Any questions, feel free to PM me on here, or you can find me on Skype as RA (pic of a bearded guy). I look forward to hearing from someone interested in running, and those of you looking for the vamp game (not the wolf one) feel free to drop a line. If this future ST feels like bringing extra folks in, power to him/her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=